---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About" description={`Why ${SITE.name} exists and how it is made.`}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><span>About</span></nav>
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{SITE.name} means “Let’s learn” in Tamil.</p>
    <p>It started when a parent in Singapore saw his son stuck on a school question: <em>“Which is the same as 74: 6 tens 4 ones, 6 tens 14 ones, or 7 tens 10 ones?”</em> Explaining with words did not help. Showing it with bundles of sticks did.</p>
    <p>So every lesson here shows an idea with real things a child already knows, lets them build it themselves, and reads every sentence aloud.</p>
    <h2>What we promise</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Free to use, with no sign-up and no child accounts.</li>
      <li>Numbers and pictures are drawn by code, so counts are always exact.</li>
      <li>At most one small ad per page, kept away from anything a child taps, only to pay for the domain.</li>
    </ul>
    {SITE.contactEmail && <p>Ideas or mistakes? Email <span>{SITE.contactEmail}</span>.</p>}
  </div>
</Base>
